From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:35:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm: skip retain on a head without a scanout buffer

A head that was never flushed has no scanout buffer, and the retain
assert aborted plymouthd in the middle of a quit. Leave such a head
alone.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 src/plugins/renderers/drm/plugin.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/renderers/drm/plugin.c b/src/plugins/renderers/drm/plugin.c
index bb94127..3f92bf8 100644
--- a/src/plugins/renderers/drm/plugin.c
+++ b/src/plugins/renderers/drm/plugin.c
@@ -787,7 +787,10 @@ ply_renderer_head_retain (ply_renderer_backend_t *backend,
 
         buffer = ply_hashtable_lookup (backend->output_buffers,
                                        (void *) (uintptr_t) head->scan_out_buffer_id);
-        assert (buffer != NULL);
+        if (buffer == NULL) {
+                ply_trace ("No scanout FB on head, nothing to retain");
+                return;
+        }
 
         ply_trace("Closing FB %u (retaining)", buffer->id);
         ret = drmModeCloseFB (backend->device_fd, buffer->id);
-- 
